,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"As indicated by its hyphenated name, Nilo-Saharan is a family of the African interior, including the greater Nile Basin and the Central Sahara Desert. Most of its proposed constituent divisions are found in the modern countries of Sudan and South Sudan, through which the Nile River flows.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
1,Nilotic peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilotic_peoples,"The signature Nilotic A and B clades were the most common paternal lineages amongst the Nilo-Saharan speakers, except those inhabiting western Sudan. There, a prominent North African influence was noted.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
2,Nilotic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilotic_languages,"The Nilotic languages are languages spoken across wide areas between Egypt, Ethiopia, Sudan, South Sudan, Democratic Republic of Congo, Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania by the Nilotic peoples.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
3,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://web.archive.org/web/20230306013112/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed family of African languages spoken by some 50–60 million people, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
4,KEIYO STAR THE MUSICIAN (mapunjan) - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/channel/UCNSoT_HOUsutLjAApBCFnmQ,"Listen to music from KEIYO STAR THE MUSICIAN (mapunjan) on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
5,"KICHAME CULTURE BY MAPUNJAN KEIYOSTAR - YouTubeKeiyo AI — Translation, Text-to-Speech & Speech Recognition ...The Marakwets and Keiyo in Music: A Socio-Cultural Study - JSTORThe pride of Keiyo by kerio stars! | Keiyo Nation - FacebookNilo-Saharan languages - WikipediaNilotic peoples - Wikipedia",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-6og0AcRXxA,"Sep 12, 2025 · KICHAME CULTURE BY MAPUNJAN KEIYOSTAR KEIYO STAR THE MUSICIAN (mapunjan) 6.73K subscribers Subscribe Subscribed Whether you need to translate content into Keiyo, generate Keiyo speech audio, or transcribe Keiyo voice recordings, Vambo AI provides the technology to do it at scale. The events which call for music-making include ""economic"" activities, such as cutting down the bush, digging the sowing or planting, harvesting, and building. One may see workers themselves singing to accompany the work. Jun 6, 2025 · What is the name of the song? Proud to be a keiyo. Sweet song. Proud of my KEIYO Family!!!.. ️ Gaa ne Gaa, Keiyo keel the Great cliff dwellers ️.. !!... Hii ni kioncho tu,...Na pado!. Creative sweet song. Haron Koech Kindly bro,...Most of Nandi men married our Keiyo daughters since time in memorial..we Keiyo's are Kamaama to most Nandi men!!... As indicated by its hyphenated name, Nilo-Saharan is a family of the African interior, including the greater Nile Basin and the Central Sahara Desert. Most of its proposed constituent divisions are found in the modern countries of Sudan and South Sudan, through which the Nile River flows. The signature Nilotic A and B clades were the most common paternal lineages amongst the Nilo-Saharan speakers, except those inhabiting western Sudan. There, a prominent North African influence was noted. Are Nilo-Saharan people related to Niger-Congo speakers? Nilotic people and other Nilo-Saharan groups are also closely related to Niger-Congo speakers of West and Central Africa. Both groups are inferred to have diverged from a common ancestor around 28,000 years ago, perhaps somewhere in the Sahel. Are Nilo-Saharan Nilotes African? According to the researchers, Nilotes generally form their own African genetic cluster, although relatively most closely related to other Nilo-Saharan populations, more distantly followed by Afro-Asiatic speakers and Niger-Congo speakers. What is the earliest written language of the Nilo-Saharan family? The earliest written language associated with the Nilo-Saharan family is Old Nubian, one of the oldest written African languages, attested in writing from the 8th to the 15th century AD. Nilo-Saharan is not accepted by all linguists.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
6,"Keiyo AI — Translation, Text-to-Speech & Speech Recognition ...",https://vambo.ai/languages/keiyo,"Whether you need to translate content into Keiyo, generate Keiyo speech audio, or transcribe Keiyo voice recordings, Vambo AI provides the technology to do it at scale.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
7,The Marakwets and Keiyo in Music: A Socio-Cultural Study - JSTOR,https://www.jstor.org/stable/1214619,"The events which call for music-making include ""economic"" activities, such as cutting down the bush, digging the sowing or planting, harvesting, and building. One may see workers themselves singing to accompany the work.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
8,The pride of Keiyo by kerio stars! | Keiyo Nation - FacebookNilo-Saharan languages - WikipediaNilotic peoples - Wikipedia,https://www.facebook.com/keiyo.nation.online/videos/the-pride-of-keiyo-by-kerio-stars/1272072254260384/,"Jun 6, 2025 · What is the name of the song? Proud to be a keiyo. Sweet song. Proud of my KEIYO Family!!!.. ️ Gaa ne Gaa, Keiyo keel the Great cliff dwellers ️.. !!... Hii ni kioncho tu,...Na pado!. Creative sweet song. Haron Koech Kindly bro,...Most of Nandi men married our Keiyo daughters since time in memorial..we Keiyo's are Kamaama to most Nandi men!!... As indicated by its hyphenated name, Nilo-Saharan is a family of the African interior, including the greater Nile Basin and the Central Sahara Desert. Most of its proposed constituent divisions are found in the modern countries of Sudan and South Sudan, through which the Nile River flows. The signature Nilotic A and B clades were the most common paternal lineages amongst the Nilo-Saharan speakers, except those inhabiting western Sudan. There, a prominent North African influence was noted. Are Nilo-Saharan people related to Niger-Congo speakers? Nilotic people and other Nilo-Saharan groups are also closely related to Niger-Congo speakers of West and Central Africa. Both groups are inferred to have diverged from a common ancestor around 28,000 years ago, perhaps somewhere in the Sahel. Are Nilo-Saharan Nilotes African? According to the researchers, Nilotes generally form their own African genetic cluster, although relatively most closely related to other Nilo-Saharan populations, more distantly followed by Afro-Asiatic speakers and Niger-Congo speakers. What is the earliest written language of the Nilo-Saharan family? The earliest written language associated with the Nilo-Saharan family is Old Nubian, one of the oldest written African languages, attested in writing from the 8th to the 15th century AD. Nilo-Saharan is not accepted by all linguists.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
9,Nilo-Saharan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/39/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..q1Sf4rd3drUq_qVbZh2jE_3soRxTIxU8lmX0apb_0eA,"Nilo-Saharan. Subgroup of 210 languages.Keiyo eyo, a language of Kenya.",Keiyo,Nilo-Saharan
